{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "002O", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-limits-products-equalizers}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c914f923cc80b66fe8a59bc70cc7f9c78b6281933492d0446aa694ff488cd9df", "source_text": "Since products, fibre products, equalizers, and final objects are limits with nonempty index categories we see that (1) implies both (2) and (3). By Lemma <REF_0001> above we see that (2) implies (1). Assume (3).", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3779c8df937ba85d3c4fe620ef67ae4f7e1fbddf390a7c8f2a063e828aefe06e", "unit_id": "tag:002O:proof-p001"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof_paragraph", "parent_tag": "002O", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A \\times B$", "MATH_0002": "$a, b : A \\to B$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$a, b$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:48bc2f02238b2704e4e03383e3f8a0e4817f8e8cc1f7d542a7f1c036b841b13c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bb0abf82835258181da111c0683ef9ddd3f8ac14ade8cb2ee13a7e02f231165b", "source_text": "Note that the product <MATH_0001> is the fibre product over the final object. If <MATH_0002> are morphisms of <MATH_0003>, then the equalizer of <MATH_0004> is", "source_text_hash": "sha256:144fcec661f93de6228a220a7f59ac9bd644ecfbdf2bbd2e774f092a1eb04796", "unit_id": "tag:002O:proof-p002"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "display_math", "parent_tag": "002O", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n(A \\times_{a, B, b} A)\\times_{(\\text{pr}_1, \\text{pr}_2), A \\times A, \\Delta} A.\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f7dc1958c33312bf12b730c1530064d8d1d2682c75ee66e4f5d0577f40970129", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f25b61ea592297117311921346716703f2fcc52cccaab219a7f540907dc8097f", "source_text": "<MATH_0001>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f624e62d0a08cb4d4f7609fd8d992c88c0c527d3d910b8338b5f898e6261de67", "unit_id": "tag:002O:display001"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof_paragraph", "parent_tag": "002O", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{proof}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bf8af82e66ad165774fcd252994a7cc41813ff4abf9658f0e69801ff9ecacec5", "source_text": "Thus (3) implies (2) and the lemma is proved.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0a7283eceaf9db399b737ac0a2dbcfec5603d2087209a529238da27318ee9520", "unit_id": "tag:002O:proof-p003"}
